","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.5.beta3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4060 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7640) - AMD Ryzen 7 7735HS with Radeon Graphics (16 threads) - 15.19 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nTileMapLayers using SVGTextures seem to ignore oversampling rules. Here's a picture with my MRP zoomed in ~5.5x, with oversampling_override set to ~5.5x\n\n<img width=\"1600\" height=\"1081\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/64019077-0865-4e10-a5d6-d8ff39f8d1df\" />\n\nThe door sprite and player AnimatedSprite look crisp, but the TileMapLayer seems to still render at 64x64. It should scale up with oversampling considering the tile itself is also using an SVGTexture.\n\n<img width=\"1304\" height=\"503\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3d2f5ab-6ea2-43f7-b393-c31bb7d6a954\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nImport an SVGTexture to use as a tile's texture and try increasing `oversampling_override`. The tiles won't change.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tilemap-svg-test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21445961/tilemap-svg-test.zip)\n\nHold up to zoom in & increase oversampling override, hold down to zoom out & decrease oversampling override.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109000/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}